# OPUS-ROOT-CALL-20260930-17: the two-argument form written above Other's declaration.  The type-word test does
# not depend on what is registered, so both walks of the lexical pass take `Other:` below as a named Structure (with
# the registration-dependent test the walks disagree about it).  At this line Other is not yet visible -- names are
# read from the statement's source position -- so since OPUS-TYPED-BINDING-20260930-20 `Model: Other extra` is the
# typed binding of an absent Other with the candidate extra, an int: refused where it stands.
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
end: Model

int: extra 1
Model: Other extra

Other:
    size_t: p 2U
end: Other
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
